    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Kyle Tucker** (70.33) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.94) serving as our primary engines. **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a high-floor matchup against Sproat, where his ability to drive production remains untethered by the pitcher's moderate xERA of 4.25. Meanwhile, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** projects as our most dangerous run-producer; despite a slight platoon dip against Keller, his elite 0.378 xwOBA and favorable #3 spot in the order make him an essential play. We are also monitoring **Gunnar Henderson** (64.90), whose score is buoyed by his #2 lineup placement and a situational boost from the pitcher's slow delivery, which enhances his stolen base potential\u2014a critical factor given our strategic emphasis on speed.\n\nDown the order, **Jackson Merrill** (61.41) provides a strong platoon-driven edge against Medina, and **Miguel Vargas** (57.67) receives a notable lift from wind conditions, which pushes his utility higher than his raw base projections. The most difficult decision rested with our bench, where **Josh Jung** (44.05) remained the final cut. While **Josh Jung** carries a respectable projection, the combination of a tough matchup against Detmers (3.23 xERA) and the uncertainty surrounding his lineup spot relegated him to the bench in favor of higher-efficiency hitters. We remain cautious regarding **Coby Mayo**, whose pending lineup status (assumed #8) and the opponent's ability to hold runners limit his ceiling to a marginal 52.47, though we are optimistic he can exploit the park factors to outperform that baseline.",
